    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Most of this chapter is focused on conditional expectation, i.e., the expectation of one variable, given information on another. For example, one may know the value of x (perhaps parental height), and wish to compute the expected value of y (offspring height) given x. In general, conditional expectations are computed by using the conditional density",
