    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "If $x$ and $y$ are independent, then $E(y|x) = E(y)$, the unconditional expectation. Otherwise, $E(y|x)$ is a function of the specified $x$ value. For height in humans (Figure 1.1), Galton (1889) observed a linear relationship,",
      "source_page": 52,
      "printed_page": 32,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p52:b17"
      ],
